WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.917
[Police Sirens Blaring]

00:00:23.812 --> 00:00:27.070
- [Mark] Alright Kevin,
Kevin where'd you grow up.

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:28.470
- I grew up in Inglewood, California.

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:30.020
- [Mark] Inglewood, okay.

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:32.870
And how long have you been
out on the street now?

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:36.400
- Uh I've been out a year, but I violated,

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:38.770
so right now I've been out eight years

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:40.860
cause I went back to jail.

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:43.091
- [Mark] But since your last prison term

00:00:43.091 --> 00:00:44.890
you've been out just a few months right?

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:46.880
- Uh yeah. Eight... Going on eight months.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:47.713
- [Mark] Eight months yeah?

00:00:47.713 --> 00:00:48.546
- Yes.

00:00:48.546 --> 00:00:49.379
- [Mark] And what were you in prison for?

00:00:49.379 --> 00:00:51.150
- Torture, aggravated mayhem.

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:52.150
- [Mark] Torture.

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:53.800
- Aggravated mayhem.

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:54.633
- [Mark] Mayhem?

00:00:54.633 --> 00:00:55.466
- Yeah.

00:00:55.466 --> 00:00:56.299
- [Mark] That's what they call it?

00:00:56.299 --> 00:00:57.510
- Torture and aggravated mayhem.

00:00:57.510 --> 00:00:58.480
- [Mark] Wow.

00:00:58.480 --> 00:00:59.313
- Yes.

00:00:59.313 --> 00:01:00.146
- [Mark] And how many
years did you get for that?

00:01:00.146 --> 00:01:01.220
- I did 22 years.

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:03.340
I got a life sentence
when I was 15 years old

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:04.173
for that crime.

00:01:04.173 --> 00:01:05.006
- [Mark] A life sentence at 15?

00:01:05.006 --> 00:01:06.470
- Yes. At 15.

00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:09.076
They charged me as an adult, bound me

00:01:09.076 --> 00:01:14.076
over to adult court and I
lost my trial was found guilty

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:16.600
for my charges and was sentenced

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:19.300
to what they call an
indeterminate life sentence

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:21.070
which was seven years to life.

00:01:21.070 --> 00:01:23.363
But I did 22 years on my life sentence.

00:01:25.838 --> 00:01:28.685
- [Mark] What were the
circumstances that got you?

00:01:28.685 --> 00:01:30.957
I mean, what was the...
what was the offense?

00:01:30.957 --> 00:01:32.410
It wasn't murder.

00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:33.740
- No, I wasn't in jail for murder.

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:36.040
I went to jail for
torture, aggravated mayhem.

00:01:37.406 --> 00:01:41.640
In 1996 I was convicted
for uh, burning uh...

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:47.913
Someone... for uh,

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:50.940
for some gang... you know.

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:53.040
Personal things that I, you
know, I, I needed to do.

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:54.820
I don't want to get into detail about that

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:58.730
but I got convicted for torturing someone

00:01:58.730 --> 00:02:01.890
for burning them with
hot spoons over his body.

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:04.940
And uh, I did 22 years for it.

00:02:04.940 --> 00:02:05.900
- [Mark] And you were in a gang?

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:06.800
- Yes, sir.

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:07.633
- [Mark] Which gang were you in?

00:02:07.633 --> 00:02:09.273
- I was part of the neighborhood Pirus.

00:02:10.210 --> 00:02:11.360
In Inglewood California.

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:12.780
- [Mark] Which is part of the Bloods?

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:13.613
- Yes.

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:17.930
- [Mark] And so that means
you didn't go to high school.

00:02:17.930 --> 00:02:19.430
- Did I go to high school?

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:21.508
I dropped out of school after elementary.

00:02:21.508 --> 00:02:22.390
- [Mark] Oh you did?

00:02:22.390 --> 00:02:23.760
- Yes.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:25.560
- [Mark] So that was even
before you went to prison.

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:27.060
- Even before I went to prison...

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:29.430
Years before I went to
prison, I was, I stopped

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:32.163
going to school. I lost
all respect for authority.

00:02:33.008 --> 00:02:35.560
I would just... I became
a juvenile delinquent.

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:37.590
I was a very bad kid.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.690
- [Mark] Tell me about your
childhood, your parents.

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:41.206
Did you have both parents growing up?

00:02:41.206 --> 00:02:44.500
- I grew up with... I grew
up in a single parent home.

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:46.990
My dad was a truck driver.
My dad was married.

00:02:46.990 --> 00:02:49.830
So, you know, he stayed in his marriage

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:53.640
and my mom, you know, raised
three, three boys by herself.

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:56.500
You know, she worked for the
post office, made good money

00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:58.870
kept a roof over our heads,
clothes over our back,

00:02:58.870 --> 00:03:00.670
and food in our stomach. She did that.

00:03:00.670 --> 00:03:01.530
That's what my mom did.

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:03.020
That's one thing I got to say

00:03:03.020 --> 00:03:08.010
that I can, my mom never,
you know, had us without.

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:10.410
We had everything, birthdays,
Christmases, Thanksgivings.

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:12.538
I had a very good life.

00:03:12.538 --> 00:03:15.770
But growing up in an environment

00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:18.280
a gang infested... gang
infested environment,

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:20.780
such as you know, where
I grew up at, you know

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:24.270
we got those negative influences
in the streets and you know

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:26.738
I became influenced, you
know, I was, you know, I was

00:03:26.738 --> 00:03:30.720
I was a little small kid
that was very talented.

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:31.553
You know what I'm saying?

00:03:31.553 --> 00:03:33.620
I knew how to play
basketball. I was funny.

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:34.650
I knew how to dance.

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:37.430
So I had a lot of friends and I, and, and

00:03:37.430 --> 00:03:39.602
and I influenced them,
you know what I'm saying?

00:03:39.602 --> 00:03:42.810
And through that talent
and that gift, but you know

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:44.520
when my behavior changed, you know

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:47.660
when I start getting high,
when I stopped going to school

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:49.780
when I stopped listening
to my mom, you know

00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:52.080
I started adopting those, those, you know

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:55.260
dysfunctional belief systems,
you know, gangs, you know

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:57.420
I want to, I wanted to
be part of the gang.

00:03:57.420 --> 00:04:00.465
I wanted to be, I want to fit
in, you know what I'm saying?

00:04:00.465 --> 00:04:01.469
I wanted to be down.

00:04:01.469 --> 00:04:03.270
And I did.

00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:05.050
I was brave enough to do that.

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:07.100
I start stealing cars.
I start smoking weed.

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:09.228
I start selling dope. I
start picking up guns.

00:04:09.228 --> 00:04:10.870
I started doing all those things

00:04:10.870 --> 00:04:12.360
juvenile delinquent kids did.

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:14.823
And I started influencing other kids.

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:16.753
I really did.

00:04:16.753 --> 00:04:18.832
I started influencing other kids.

00:04:18.832 --> 00:04:19.762
- [Mark] They looked up to you.

00:04:19.762 --> 00:04:20.595
- They looked up to me, they looked

00:04:20.595 --> 00:04:23.040
up to me and my twin brother,
you know what I'm saying?

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:24.430
We, my mom kept us with money.

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:27.575
My dad, even when he came
by he kept us with money,

00:04:27.575 --> 00:04:28.890
you know?

00:04:28.890 --> 00:04:31.513
And it's not to take away
from, you know, any other

00:04:31.513 --> 00:04:34.120
did the other kids that
was negative influence.

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:36.650
And it, you know, we, we, we, you know

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:38.270
I had some friends that I looked up to

00:04:38.270 --> 00:04:39.380
you know what I'm saying?

00:04:39.380 --> 00:04:40.970
But I had some people who really looked

00:04:40.970 --> 00:04:44.420
up to me and they really,
and they really followed me.

00:04:44.420 --> 00:04:47.790
They really, you know,
was allowing me to, to

00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:50.090
to be a negative influence on them.

00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:51.393
And, and I regret it.

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:53.243
No what I'm saying

00:04:53.243 --> 00:04:57.673
I lost my life at 15
years old, I got life.

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:01.960
And I didn't even understand
how serious it was

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:02.793
at that time.

00:05:02.793 --> 00:05:04.010
You know what I'm saying?

00:05:04.010 --> 00:05:06.350
Because I was a hurt kid, you know

00:05:06.350 --> 00:05:08.690
no one never really understood that.

00:05:08.690 --> 00:05:09.523
You know what I'm saying?

00:05:09.523 --> 00:05:11.810
I was, I had all these gifts,
I had all these talents

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:13.256
but I was a hurt kid.

00:05:13.256 --> 00:05:15.212
You find what I'm saying
that, I love my mom.

00:05:15.212 --> 00:05:16.730
You know what I'm saying?

00:05:16.730 --> 00:05:18.810
I wanted a dad, you know what I'm saying?

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:20.447
Me and my twin, you know, we had a...

00:05:20.447 --> 00:05:23.513
we loved each other, but our
relationship was dysfunctional.

00:05:23.513 --> 00:05:24.346
You know what I'm saying?

00:05:24.346 --> 00:05:26.300
But we love each other. We
used to fight about everything.

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:28.240
Everybody know that.
So it ain't no secret,

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:30.900
but you know what I'm saying? It was just,

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:32.620
I wanted to fit in. I wanted to be,

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:34.167
I wanted to fit in and I didn't.

00:05:34.167 --> 00:05:36.340
And a lot of people didn't
even understand that.

00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:39.570
I was the one that I was
really seeking the approval.

00:05:39.570 --> 00:05:40.757
You know what I'm saying.

00:05:40.757 --> 00:05:43.710
And that led those belief
systems that I adopted.

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:46.280
You know what I'm saying,
led me to get life

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:49.940
in prison at 15 years
old, that wasn't normal.

00:05:49.940 --> 00:05:51.816
You didn't hear in 1996

00:05:51.816 --> 00:05:55.844
a kid getting life in
prison, that wasn't normal.

00:05:55.844 --> 00:05:59.880
And that's because the gang
epidemic has grew so much

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:01.520
to where we was destroying
our communities.

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:02.510
A lot of people was down.

00:06:02.510 --> 00:06:04.260
So they was changing
laws and it was coming

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:08.790
down hard on gang members
and Los Angeles, Pete Wilson

00:06:08.790 --> 00:06:10.290
and all these law makers.

00:06:10.290 --> 00:06:12.180
And, you know, these are
the things that I found

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:13.160
out throughout the years, you know

00:06:13.160 --> 00:06:14.441
when I was studying in prison

00:06:14.441 --> 00:06:16.820
and learning about myself and learning how

00:06:16.820 --> 00:06:18.140
to get out of prison.

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:23.140
But, you know, I got life
at 15 and, and it, it, it

00:06:23.240 --> 00:06:27.423
I didn't even understand
the seriousness of it.

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:29.550
I was so childish.

00:06:29.550 --> 00:06:30.509
I was so immature.

00:06:30.509 --> 00:06:33.683
I was so naive as a kid
cause I was a child.

00:06:33.683 --> 00:06:37.619
It was, it was, it happened so fast to me.

00:06:37.619 --> 00:06:40.730
You know, I had my mom who
was hurt that I was even

00:06:40.730 --> 00:06:43.890
in that situation, she
couldn't understand it either.

00:06:43.890 --> 00:06:44.723
You know?

00:06:44.723 --> 00:06:48.490
And you know, they, they gave me life

00:06:49.570 --> 00:06:52.590
and I remembered the day I got life.

00:06:52.590 --> 00:06:56.840
I walked into Tulare's court,
municipal court, adult court

00:06:56.840 --> 00:06:59.510
holding tank, after I got found guilty,

00:06:59.510 --> 00:07:01.264
got sentenced to life.

00:07:01.264 --> 00:07:04.813
I told myself, I would
never get out of jail again.

00:07:05.733 --> 00:07:08.960
I was 15 years old telling myself that

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:11.670
because I already, now, I

00:07:11.670 --> 00:07:14.803
they made me understand my situation.

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:17.117
You understand what I'm saying?

00:07:17.117 --> 00:07:19.900
And I went into CDC.

00:07:19.900 --> 00:07:24.080
I went into prison, to
department of corrections

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:25.505
already knowing and believing

00:07:25.505 --> 00:07:28.033
as a child that I was
never getting out of jail.

00:07:29.380 --> 00:07:32.953
So I lost hope right then and there

00:07:32.953 --> 00:07:34.203
you know what I'm saying?

00:07:35.101 --> 00:07:39.160
And... I watched my mom deteriorate

00:07:41.981 --> 00:07:44.660
but I still didn't see it.

00:07:44.660 --> 00:07:49.470
I didn't see the pain I
caused my mother, you know

00:07:49.470 --> 00:07:53.920
not just to myself, my mother, you know,

00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:54.870
but most of all

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:57.770
I ain't even understand
what I did to my victim

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:02.653
the pain I caused him
because of the life I chose.

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:05.050
You know what I'm saying?

00:08:05.050 --> 00:08:07.139
If I wouldn't never been a gang member

00:08:07.139 --> 00:08:08.760
I would never did that.

00:08:08.760 --> 00:08:11.280
I would never did life in prison.

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:13.500
And that's what that ultimately comes

00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:16.380
down to for me as a man, growing

00:08:16.380 --> 00:08:20.187
up as a man and understanding
my responsibility in my world.

00:08:20.187 --> 00:08:22.010
And the choices I made in my life

00:08:22.010 --> 00:08:25.429
and where I'm at right now,
just because I chose gangs.

00:08:25.429 --> 00:08:27.680
- [Mark] What do you think
helped you make that decision?

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:29.586
Is it not having your
dad around all the time?

00:08:29.586 --> 00:08:32.373
Was it, was it just the kids
in the neighborhood, friends?

00:08:32.373 --> 00:08:34.390
- It was all the above.

00:08:34.390 --> 00:08:35.730
It was not having my dad around.

00:08:35.730 --> 00:08:37.850
I grew up in a single
parent home where my mom

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:38.690
was worked all the time.

00:08:38.690 --> 00:08:39.523
She never was at home.

00:08:39.523 --> 00:08:41.300
She couldn't, she couldn't control us.

00:08:41.300 --> 00:08:42.850
I had so much free time as a child

00:08:42.850 --> 00:08:45.784
to where as soon as I
step outside, there we go.

00:08:45.784 --> 00:08:48.300
And my mom, you know, she spoiled us.

00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:50.180
So she gave us a lot of freedom

00:08:50.180 --> 00:08:53.800
and we took advantage of it,
straight up, bottom line.

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:56.350
I took advantage of the
freedom that my mom gave me

00:08:56.350 --> 00:08:59.360
as a good mother and I
brought pain to her life.

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:02.210
I brought pain to my life
and ultimately I brought pain

00:09:02.210 --> 00:09:03.260
to my victims life.

00:09:04.107 --> 00:09:06.053
And I regret every bit of it.

00:09:07.311 --> 00:09:10.500
And I had to do 22 years in prison.

00:09:10.500 --> 00:09:11.360
I had to suffer.

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:14.787
I had to, I had to learn how
to become a man in prison

00:09:14.787 --> 00:09:19.787
and I suffered. God and, and,
humanity put me through it.

00:09:19.900 --> 00:09:22.100
It was part of, it was part of my growth.

00:09:22.100 --> 00:09:23.803
It was part of me being held accountable

00:09:23.803 --> 00:09:26.500
for the choices that I did.

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:27.400
You know, I got hurt.

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:28.233
I hurt people.

00:09:28.233 --> 00:09:29.990
I've been, I've been held accountable.

00:09:29.990 --> 00:09:32.888
I been in trouble after I
got it, got life in prison.

00:09:32.888 --> 00:09:34.310
That's why I did 22 years.

00:09:34.310 --> 00:09:36.620
The first time I was
eligible for parole was 2003.

00:09:36.620 --> 00:09:39.740
I could have got out, but I
was so caught up into gangs.

00:09:39.740 --> 00:09:42.360
I was so caught up into the
lifestyle to where I was.

00:09:42.360 --> 00:09:43.500
I didn't have no home.

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:46.540
I didn't want to come
home because I was content

00:09:46.540 --> 00:09:48.685
with spending the rest of my life in jail.

00:09:48.685 --> 00:09:53.230
But when I lost my mother,
when I lost my mother

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:58.230
on her death bed, she
asked me to change my life.

00:09:59.996 --> 00:10:03.578
But it wasn't that, she
asked my big brother

00:10:03.578 --> 00:10:05.673
to get me out of jail.

00:10:06.652 --> 00:10:10.230
And my big brother tried,
and let me say this.

00:10:10.230 --> 00:10:13.670
My big brother, my big brother
tried his best to get me

00:10:13.670 --> 00:10:16.753
out of prison, but he couldn't.

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:19.453
I was guilty for what I did.

00:10:20.980 --> 00:10:22.773
I had to get myself out of prison.

00:10:23.780 --> 00:10:24.613
I had to do...

00:10:24.613 --> 00:10:28.400
I had to do the big major work.

00:10:28.400 --> 00:10:30.053
I had to change my life.

00:10:30.930 --> 00:10:34.070
I had to walk away from gangs.

00:10:34.070 --> 00:10:36.640
That's what my whole life was about.

00:10:36.640 --> 00:10:37.960
I had to walk away from it

00:10:37.960 --> 00:10:40.590
in order for me to regain my life sentence

00:10:40.590 --> 00:10:43.704
to get an opportunity to live
back out in the free world.

00:10:43.704 --> 00:10:45.430
I had to walk away from gangs.

00:10:45.430 --> 00:10:47.813
I had to choose gangs or my freedom.

00:10:50.330 --> 00:10:51.550
I did that already.

00:10:51.550 --> 00:10:54.000
I gave my life to it already.

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:59.000
I owe God, my victim,

00:11:00.008 --> 00:11:04.730
my family, my community, and myself.

00:11:04.730 --> 00:11:08.470
I deserved, I deserved
another chance I had to do it.

00:11:08.470 --> 00:11:11.880
I had to give myself another
chance and I walked away

00:11:11.880 --> 00:11:14.980
from it. And it took me
years to get out of prison

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:17.710
because I had to change my belief system.

00:11:17.710 --> 00:11:19.340
Gangs is a lifestyle.

00:11:19.340 --> 00:11:20.700
That's what a lot of
people don't understand.

00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:23.180
It's a lifestyle. It's a way of thinking.

00:11:23.180 --> 00:11:24.440
You understand what I'm saying?

00:11:24.440 --> 00:11:28.200
And I had no choice, but
to go through the process

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:31.400
of changing my belief system,
adopting new belief systems.

